            Buy the <strong class="text-white">conventional vacuum first</strong> — it is the machine that can do everything, including the stairs and the sofa a robot will never touch. Add a <strong class="text-white">robot</strong> when the chore you resent is the daily floor pass rather than the fortnightly deep clean.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then let each do its job: <strong class="text-white">the robot daily on a schedule, the upright weekly on carpet, stairs and edges</strong>. That division is why households with both stop thinking about their floors at all.
          </p>
